# Verifying JSON in Python
Check if the output is valid JSON using Python:

import json

data = '''
[
  {"city": "Tokyo", "population": 13960000},
  {"city": "Lagos", "population": 15000000},
  {"city": "New York", "population": 8419000}
]
'''

parsed = json.loads(data)

print(type(parsed))
print(parsed[0]["city"])

If the JSON is invalid → Python will throw an error.
If valid it loads successfully.